<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandra Shekhar Azad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1906">1906</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Chandrashekhar Azad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chandra Shekhar Azad was an Indian revolutionary, born at Bhabhra in the princely state of Alirajpur. He took part in the Kakori train robbery of 1925 and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindustan">Hindustan</a> Socialist Republican Association with Bhagat Singh. Surrounded by police in Alfred Park, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Allahabad</a>, in February 1931, he shot himself rather than be captured, and he is honoured as a hero of the independence movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandra-shekhar-azad.jpg" alt="Chandra Shekhar Azad" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandrasekhar_Azad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
